\import{base-macros}

\p{Updated on 2026-11-24 in session [ses-ZW59](ses-ZW59) ([log-I6C0](log-I6C0)) after closing both remaining main-path lemmas and reorganising the tree for issue \issue{22}.}

\p{\strong{The proof is complete.} \code{\verb~|expf_correctlyRounded~} in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf.lean~} proves that \code{\verb~|math::double_eval::expf~}, extracted from LLVM libc at \code{\verb~|e1a5f92db023~}, is correctly rounded across all \code{\verb~|2³²~} binary32 inputs in all four rounding directions of C and reaches no operation that C++ leaves undefined. It uses zero \code{\verb~|sorry~}, zero \code{\verb~|native_decide~}, and depends solely on the three standard Lean axioms \code{\verb~|[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]~}.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Inputs}\th{Bit patterns}\th{Share}\th{State}}
\tr{\td{Zeros, infinities, NaNs, magnitude at most 2⁻²⁶, overflow, underflow}\td{3 749 616 693}\td{87.30 \%}\td{proved, \code{\verb~|Expf/ShortPaths/Ranges.lean~}}}
\tr{\td{Tiny and near-underflow main-path ranges}\td{25 256 675}\td{0.59 \%}\td{proved analytically, \code{\verb~|Expf/MainPath/ProductError.lean~}}}
\tr{\td{Main polynomial ranges (2⁻²⁴ ≤ x < 88.72…, -103.97… < x < -2⁻²⁵)}\td{520 093 927}\td{12.11 \%}\td{proved via error bound + 278 619 Chebyshev SLZ TMD certificates (\code{\verb~|Expf/MainPath/Tmd/~}) + 103 pointwise exceptions (\code{\verb~|PointwiseExceptions.lean~})}}
}

\p{\strong{How the main path is proved.} By numerical analysis and kernel-verified TMD certificates ([prob-48KJ](prob-48KJ), closed; [ins-NHOJ](ins-NHOJ)). The function-independent layers live in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Analysis/{RangeReduction,Horner,RoundingTransfer,ChebTmd}.lean~} for reuse by future functions ([note-adding-a-function](note-adding-a-function)).}

\p{\strong{What the statement rests on.} The translation by \code{\verb~|ast2lean~} and the definitions of \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Libc/~}, which are tested against the compiled code and not proved; FloatLib's model of IEEE 754 arithmetic. \code{\verb~|errno~} and the exception flags are outside the statement: [prob-VR5Z](prob-VR5Z).}

\p{\strong{Other plans.} \code{\verb~|double_eval_fma~}, \code{\verb~|static_rounding~}, \code{\verb~|integer_eval~}, and \code{\verb~|float_eval_cr_rn~} carry correctness statements in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf/Statement.lean~}. The short paths of \code{\verb~|double_eval_fma~} (87.30 \%), \code{\verb~|static_rounding~} (87.69 \%), and \code{\verb~|integer_eval~} (87.69 \%, via \code{\verb~|integerEval_eq_staticRounding_nearest~}) are proved in \code{\verb~|Expf/ShortPaths/~} with conditional reductions in \code{\verb~|LibcMath/Expf.lean~}; their main polynomial ranges remain open.}
